  --estimate N         Point estimate
  --label "..."        Add a label
  --description "..."  Story description
  --owner-ids N,...    Comma-separated user IDs to assign as owners. The API
                       ignores owners on create, so this fires a follow-up
                       update automatically.

Story Update Flags:
  --state STATE      State: unscheduled, unstarted, planned, started, finished, delivered, rejected, accepted
  --estimate N       Point estimate
  --owner-ids N,...  Comma-separated user IDs

Story Label Flags:
  --label "..."      Label name (required)

Story Comment Flags:
  --text "..."       Comment text (required)

Cache Sync Flags:
  Default behavior: unfiltered pagination — works on every project. The
  server-side filter DSL (--active, --state, etc.) is much faster on
  small/well-indexed projects, but on large/legacy projects the filtered
  endpoint times out at the LT 30s server-side gateway limit, so it is
  opt-in.

  --active               Sweep ACTIVE_STATES server-side (one request per
                         state in unstarted, planned, started, finished,
                         delivered, rejected). Skips accepted + icebox.
                         Fast when the LT filter endpoint works for this
                         project; may 504 on large/legacy projects.
  --state STATE          Single-state sweep using ?filter=state:<state>.
  --exclude-state S      Single sweep using ?filter=-state:<state>.
  --type TYPE            Single sweep using ?filter=type:<type>.
  --label NAME           Single sweep using ?filter=label:<name>.
  --filter "<dsl>"       Raw single-clause filter DSL passthrough.
